Introduction (5 min): Teacher will go over the drama exercise from yesterday and discuss the conflicts between China and Britain.

Theater exercise (30 min): Students will act out a scene from the Opium Wars. The scene will include the following characters: a British soldier, a Chinese official, a Chinese peasant, and an opium addict. The scene will start with the British soldier entering a Chinese village and approaching a Chinese official. The British soldier will demand the Chinese official to surrender. The Chinese official will refuse and a fight will break out between the British soldier and the Chinese official. A Chinese peasant will try to stop the fight but will get injured. An opium addict will appear and beg the British soldier for opium. The British soldier will refuse at first but then give in to the addict’s plea and give him opium. The addict will become violent and attack the Chinese official. The British soldier will try to stop the addict but will get injured as well. The scene will end with the British soldier leaving the village.

